  "why": "Every claimed complete proof is set aside. Cerdá was withdrawn. Sabihi carries specific errors that no one has answered. Sultan is an unread viXra claim with no uptake, while later papers still call the problem open. Results conditional on abc or Szpiro (Overholt, Dąbrowski, Luca, Bolvardizadeh, and Lakovskiy's Lean proof) are reductions to unproven hypotheses, so they score 'none'; F7 also applies to the Lean check. Computer searches score 'instances'. Takeda's finite-field result, Agama, Venkat and Novaković change the question, so they are variants. Two in-window results restrict the class of x and settle the equation there: Naciri (x±1 7-free or a prime power, which yields 4, 5, 7) and Bravo (x Padovan or Perrin, which yields (4,5)). Both are cases, and both confirm the conjecture. I counted Naciri as digested because Integers is a journal of record. The close call was Bravo: a case, or a variant? The equation is unchanged and only the range of x is restricted, so I chose case, though the restriction is thin. Maiti's finiteness claim would not answer the statement anyway, so it scores none.",
